Not submitted upstream.
llama-pinned-copy-stream.patch v2, 2026-11-11. Base: llama.cpp master 7592b61d3. Apply: git apply llama-pinned-copy-stream.patch
(adds ggml/src/ggml-cuda/weight-stream.cu/.cuh: re-run cmake so the CUDA glob picks them up)
Design
  Prefill with experts in host RAM (-cmoe / -ncmoe). In llama_context::sched_copy_experts, a MUL_MAT_ID host weight
  whose ids cover >= LLAMA_WS_MIN_TOKENS (1024) tokens is uploaded whole, without reading the ids back (no sync), by a
  CUDA-backend weight streamer (proc addresses ggml_backend_cuda_ws_prefetch / _consume / _pin / _stats). One worker
  thread issues cudaMemcpyAsync on its own copy stream into a private device slot (4 slots); the compute stream waits
  on the slot's event and copies slot -> sched dst (D2D, ~1% of time). The order of host weights from the previous
  large graph is kept, so the next weights upload while the current split computes (wraps into the next ubatch).
  Source of each upload:
    v2  LLAMA_WS_PIN_GIB=<GiB> (default 0 = off): at context creation the host *_exps tensors are copied once, whole,
        in layer order, into one cudaHostAlloc arena of min(budget, host expert bytes); those DMA straight from it.
    v1  everything else: memcpy mmap -> pinned ring (1 MiB x 8 = 8 MiB, stays in L3) -> DMA.
  Small batches (decode) take the unchanged stock path. LLAMA_WS=0 disables all of it. Other env: GGML_CUDA_WS_RING_MIB,
  GGML_CUDA_WS_CHUNK_KIB, GGML_CUDA_WS_SLOTS, GGML_CUDA_WS_THREADS, GGML_CUDA_WS_PAGEABLE, GGML_CUDA_WS_STATS.
Measured (RTX 5090 PCIe, Ryzen 5800X, 31 GB, a MoE GGUF (IQ1_M), -t 8 -b 4096 -ub 4096 --cache-ram 0, cold
unique-nonce, engine prompt tok/s, median of 3 reps x 2 passes; wall within 1%)
                 2.7k: stock / v1 / v2 best (budget)       10k: stock / v1 / v2 best (budget)
  -ncmoe 12      2,016 / 2,480 / 2,907 (8; all 5.4 GiB)     2,757 / 3,739 / 4,352 (8)  = 1.58x stock
  -ncmoe 18      1,602 / 2,056 / 2,461 (12; all 8.2 GiB)    2,236 / 3,175 / 3,897 (12) = 1.74x
  -ncmoe 24      1,292 / 1,689 / 2,057 (12; all 11.1 GiB)   1,844 / 2,742 / 3,527 (12) = 1.91x
  -cmoe          720 / 1,000 / 1,046 (4)                    1,082 / 1,703 / 1,797 (4)  = 1.66x
  -cmoe with 8 / 12 GiB pinned COLLAPSES (10k 747 / 303, 2.7k 204 / 98; 18-42k major faults per request): on 31 GB
  the page cache can no longer hold the unpinned experts + the 28.8 GB n-gram mmap. Keep -cmoe pins <= 4 GiB here.
  nsys -ncmoe 12 v2 PIN 8, 10k (4,297 tok/s): 17.4 GB pinned H2D on the copy stream at 28.7 GB/s (87% of H2D), 62% of it
  under kernels, kernel duty 63%. v1 -cmoe 10k: 19.2 GB/s, 27% overlap, duty 20%. Decode (-cmoe, 128 tok): unchanged.
Correctness: greedy --temp 0, 96 tokens, 4 prompts 2.6k-9.1k tokens: byte-identical to stock (v1, and v2 at PIN 12).
